								<div id="contentForThisGame_ctn">
				</div>
									<div data-panel="{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;PanelGroup&quot;}" id="aboutThisGame" class="game_page_autocollapse" style="max-height: 850px;">
						<div id="game_area_description" class="game_area_description">
							<h2>About This Game</h2>
							<p class="bb_paragraph" ><span class="bb_img_ctn"><video class="bb_img" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/5142680/extras/4ea3a3bf27540e98fad9179fbcfa3d7b.poster.avif?t=1794351394" aria-label="EXPIRATION — The only way out is through" width=1170 height=600 ><source src="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/5142680/extras/4ea3a3bf27540e98fad9179fbcfa3d7b.mp4?t=1794351394" type="video/mp4"></video></span></p><p class="bb_paragraph" ><strong>Meet EXPIRATION — a first-person psychological horror strategy game where diabetes management becomes a deadly table duel of numbers, limited resources and hidden information.</strong></p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Measure your blood glucose. Set your insulin dose. Eat when you must. Watch the numbers. Read your opponent.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ><strong>Beat the Doctor Dealer — and take the cure. </strong>Or give up before you even try.</p><h2 class="bb_tag" >WELCOME TO THE TABLE<br><span class="bb_img_ctn"><video class="bb_img" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/5142680/extras/b8815c2e3a2ac1d1d25d6103c37a1b8a.poster.avif?t=1794351394" width=1170 height=512 ><source src="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/5142680/extras/b8815c2e3a2ac1d1d25d6103c37a1b8a.mp4?t=1794351394" type="video/mp4"></video></span></h2><p class="bb_paragraph" >You wake up in a quiet hospital with no clear way out.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Across the table sits the <strong>Doctor Dealer</strong>.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Between you: insulin pens, glucose strips, food, medicine, a medical bag, monitors, papers and a clock. At first, the rules sound almost reassuring.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Keep your blood glucose under control. Use what you have. Survive. React before it is too late.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Then the Doctor Dealer takes his turn.</p><h2 class="bb_tag" >DIABETES BECOMES STRATEGY<br><span class="bb_img_ctn"><video class="bb_img" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/5142680/extras/6dceebe8f13972504912ec71b4ddd37c.poster.avif?t=1794351394" width=1170 height=512 ><source src="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/5142680/extras/6dceebe8f13972504912ec71b4ddd37c.mp4?t=1794351394" type="video/mp4"></video></span></h2><p class="bb_paragraph" >Your condition is not a conventional health bar. You have to <strong>measure it, interpret it and manage it</strong>.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Rapid and basal insulin behave differently over time. Food pushes glucose upward. Previous doses continue affecting future turns. Too much insulin can send you toward dangerous hypoglycemia; too little can leave you climbing toward severe hyperglycemia, ketones and ketoacidosis.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >A decision that looks safe now may become the problem you have to solve several turns later.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Learn the game's diabetes-management system, understand what the numbers are telling you, and decide how much risk you are willing to carry forward.</p><h2 class="bb_tag" >THE TABLE IS YOUR INTERFACE<br><span class="bb_img_ctn"><video class="bb_img" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/5142680/extras/787aa4f5e1ae3ead813df51279cdc14d.poster.avif?t=1794351394" width=1170 height=512 ><source src="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/5142680/extras/787aa4f5e1ae3ead813df51279cdc14d.mp4?t=1794351394" type="video/mp4"></video></span></h2><p class="bb_paragraph" >There is no traditional inventory screen between you and the game — only the physical objects in front of you.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Pick up an insulin pen and set the dose yourself. Insert a strip into the glucometer and wait for the result. Open the medical bag. Handle food and emergency supplies. Read monitors and physical devices. Inspect documents. Commit your turn through the objects sitting on the table.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ><strong>The table is your interface, your resource pool, your treatment — or your slow execution — and your battlefield for freedom.</strong></p><h2 class="bb_tag" >FACE THE DOCTOR DEALER<br><span class="bb_img_ctn"><video class="bb_img" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/5142680/extras/2d4d24ac527fe8648e0c6a0811b9b40e.poster.avif?t=1794351394" width=1170 height=512 ><source src="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/5142680/extras/2d4d24ac527fe8648e0c6a0811b9b40e.mp4?t=1794351394" type="video/mp4"></video></span></h2><p class="bb_paragraph" >The Doctor Dealer exists inside the same fundamental system you do.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >During competitive encounters, both sides manage their own condition, supplies and opportunities. Items that keep you alive can also become tactical tools. A valuable resource can save you, deny the Dealer an advantage — or cross the table and become somebody else's problem.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >But you will not always know the whole story.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Some information is visible. Some values are hidden. You may understand <strong>what</strong> the Doctor Dealer has done without knowing exactly <strong>how much</strong>.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >An injection may be a blank — or a real dose of insulin.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Watch his actions. Remember what has already happened. Decide what he knows about you.</p><h2 class="bb_tag" >OPEN THE BAG<br><span class="bb_img_ctn"><video class="bb_img" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/5142680/extras/888022dfe48bb6f04c1e704e0eb01b46.poster.avif?t=1794351394" width=1170 height=512 ><source src="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/5142680/extras/888022dfe48bb6f04c1e704e0eb01b46.mp4?t=1794351394" type="video/mp4"></video></span></h2><p class="bb_paragraph" >When your options begin to disappear, a medical bag can change everything.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >It may contain exactly what you need.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Or almost nothing.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Random supplies create new possibilities, but every choice changes the position at the table — and time keeps moving. Learn when another chance is worth taking, and when greed is simply another way to lose.</p><h2 class="bb_tag" >NO FLOATING HUD<br><span class="bb_img_ctn"><video class="bb_img" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/5142680/extras/b28f0e57cde3051a3d3d5442fd7adc3d.poster.avif?t=1794351394" width=1170 height=512 ><source src="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/5142680/extras/b28f0e57cde3051a3d3d5442fd7adc3d.mp4?t=1794351394" type="video/mp4"></video></span></h2><p class="bb_paragraph" >EXPIRATION is built around a diegetic interface. The information that matters lives inside the world: on glucometers, clocks, monitors, papers and the physical objects around you.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Instead of watching abstract icons, you learn to read the room itself.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Where is the insulin? What has already been used? What is still acting inside you? What can you afford to spend? What might the Doctor Dealer be hiding?</p><h2 class="bb_tag" >A SHORT, FOCUSED NIGHTMARE<br><span class="bb_img_ctn"><video class="bb_img" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/5142680/extras/9e8954e75207a174d338e7229c3124da.poster.avif?t=1794351394" width=1170 height=512 ><source src="https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/5142680/extras/9e8954e75207a174d338e7229c3124da.mp4?t=1794351394" type="video/mp4"></video></span></h2><p class="bb_paragraph" >EXPIRATION combines psychological horror, strategy, resource management and immersive first-person interaction into a compact single-player experience built around one increasingly dangerous set of rules.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >You can build a careful plan over several turns — and watch a single medical bag delivery overturn the position for either side.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Learn the table.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Manage the numbers.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" >Survive the treatment.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ><strong>Beat the Doctor Dealer.</strong></p><p class="bb_paragraph" ><strong>Take the cure.</strong></p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><p class="bb_paragraph" ><i>EXPIRATION is a fictional strategy game and is not intended as medical advice or as a substitute for real diabetes care.</i></p>						</div>
					</div>
